module gunbc.transport_shell_wall_deadline_interpreter_seed_growth

import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import std.types { String }
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }

// Seed-growth obligation for the HAND RUST this program puts in the v1 seed INTERPRETER, as distinct
// from the grammar field row (gunbc.transport_shell_wall_deadline_field_seed_growth, gunb-ai/gunbc#16842)
// that admits the declared `wall_deadline:` field itself. Two obligations, two rows: one is a roster
// field, this one is the runtime that arms a kill from that field and reports an overrun as a value.
//
// WHAT THE SUBJECT IS. The seed interpreter's shell leg: the transport node is dispatched in
// dispatch_shell, the child is waited on by wait_child_honoring_wall_deadline, the group is killed by
// kill_shell_process_group, and the observation is turned into the interpreter's ShellResult by
// shell_result_from_capture / shell_evidence_value. shell_result_of_observation is also touched, but its
// hand growth is already claimed by gunbc.modeled_operation_realization_seed_growth, and the roster refuses
// a declaration claimed twice (seed_growth_roster_has_duplicate_keys), so this row names the item in prose and
// leaves the key with that row. Before this change
// the seed had ONE bound, the whole-call wall_clock_limit, and no per-leg ceiling at all: a fleet leg
// that hung held the transport open until the whole call's bound tripped, and the fleet corpus had no
// way to say how long one leg may take.
//
// WHAT WAS ADMITTED. The seed now reads the ceiling from the transport DECLARATION (declared_shell_leg_ceiling),
// arms the process-group kill only where a declaration exists, and returns an overrun as a value
// (ShellLegExec::Overran { wall_deadline_seconds }) that the .dag transport wrappers decode into their
// own non-success arm. No 0-means-none, no exit-124 sentinel, and no InterpError for an overrun: an
// overrun is a fact about the leg, not a fault in the program. A transport that does not declare the
// field keeps main's behaviour byte for byte.
//
// WHY ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing): by PURPOSE,
// under the recorded ruling gunbc.design_ruling.v1_seed_growth_for_declared_transport_ceiling_admitted,
// which carries the operator's words, the principal and the date; this row cites that record and does
// not restate it. WHAT THE PURPOSIVE TEST ACTUALLY PASSES: the change removes a second, unmodeled
// authority rather than adding a capability. Review 96999 (REQUEST_CHANGES) is what moved the ceiling
// from a parameter spelling (param_env.lookup(ctx.sym("wall_deadline"))) into the transport
// declaration, where a caller that names a parameter by accident no longer arms a kill and a caller
// that means a ceiling must declare one. It adds no language behaviour: no new syntax beyond the
// admitted field, no flag, no new error kind.
//
// HOW THE CLAIM IS EXECUTED, NOT ASSERTED. mod wall_deadline_kill_tests holds the red/green pair:
// green_leg_under_per_leg_deadline_exits_zero_not_overran and per_leg_deadline_trip_is_overran_within_bound
// (a leg under its ceiling is Completed, a tripped ceiling is Overran carrying that ceiling),
// the_ceiling_is_the_transport_declaration_not_a_parameter_spelling (a caller that merely NAMES a
// parameter wall_deadline arms nothing), group_is_armed_only_where_a_ceiling_exists (an undeclared
// transport behaves as main's does) and drain_stall_on_overrun_never_returns_error (the overrun path
// cannot turn into an interpreter error). mod map_shell_outputs_optional_stream_tests covers the
// channel shape the overrun travels through. The .dag side of the same fact is executed by
// test.claim.live_deploy.deployed_tree_leg_deadline_witness: the incident leg (deployed_tree_leg,
// git rev-parse HEAD, ProbeLeg) overrunning maps to TreeLegDeadlineExceeded and writes a receipt.
data transport_shell_wall_deadline_interpreter_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "ShellResult", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "dispatch_shell", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "declared_shell_leg_ceiling", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "wait_child_honoring_wall_deadline", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "kill_shell_process_group", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "shell_result_from_capture", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "shell_evidence_value", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "ShellLegExec", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "settle_shell_stdin_writer", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "SHELL_STDIN_SETTLE_GRACE", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.argv_arg_limit_test", decl_name: "dispatch_shell_stdin_leg_with_escaped_pipe_holder_still_returns_the_typed_overrun", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.argv_arg_limit_test", decl_name: "dispatch_shell_stdin_leg_under_a_generous_ceiling_completes_with_its_payload_written", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.argv_arg_limit_test", decl_name: "dispatch_shell_stdin_leg_whose_child_never_reads_is_a_completion_not_an_error", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.argv_arg_limit_test", decl_name: "outer_budget_refusal_with_an_escaped_stderr_holder_returns_within_bound", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_compiler_emit", decl_name: "ShellChanOverran", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_compiler_emit", decl_name: "ShellChanWallDeadlineSeconds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.wall_deadline_kill_tests", decl_name: "the_ceiling_is_the_transport_declaration_not_a_parameter_spelling", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.wall_deadline_kill_tests", decl_name: "per_leg_deadline_trip_is_overran_within_bound", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.wall_deadline_kill_tests", decl_name: "green_leg_under_per_leg_deadline_exits_zero_not_overran", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.wall_deadline_kill_tests", decl_name: "group_is_armed_only_where_a_ceiling_exists", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.wall_deadline_kill_tests", decl_name: "drain_stall_on_overrun_never_returns_error", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter.map_shell_outputs_optional_stream_tests", decl_name: "optional_stdout_surfaces_text_on_success", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "The per-leg wall-clock ceiling cannot be expressed above the seed: arming the process-group kill from the transport declaration and returning an overrun as a value are both inside the interpreter's own shell dispatch, which is hand Rust. Admitted by PURPOSE under the recorded ruling gunbc.design_ruling.v1_seed_growth_for_declared_transport_ceiling_admitted (the operator's 2026-11-21 ruling answering review 97148), because the change retires a second unmodeled authority instead of adding a capability: review 96999 refused the version where the seed armed the kill by looking up a PARAMETER NAME, so the bound existed only where a spelling matched. The overrun is a sum arm (ShellLegExec::Overran), never an InterpError, never exit 124, never 0-means-none, and a transport that declares no ceiling keeps main's behaviour byte for byte. The three obligations this change acquired AFTER its first form are declared here too, so no hand Rust in the seed is unaccounted for: ShellLegExec, the coproduct that replaced the earlier overran Bool plus optional-deadline pair review 96705 refused because an overrun could omit its deadline; settle_shell_stdin_writer with SHELL_STDIN_SETTLE_GRACE, which bounds the stdin writer's completion so an escaped setsid descendant holding the pipe open cannot keep the transport open past the kill it already received; and the compiled path's ShellChanOverran / ShellChanWallDeadlineSeconds channels, admitted as channels only, because what the compiled backend does with them remains the guarantee gunbc.guarantee_stall.compiled_shell_leg_deadline_enforcement_stall records as missing.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Dissolves when the seed interpreter's shell dispatch is re-authored as modeled .dag over a transport whose dispatch is a modeled operation -- i.e. when ShellLegExec and the kill arming live in a .dag transport authority and the seed only executes it, at which point every DeclarationRef listed here is deleted rather than maintained. What does NOT dissolve them: adding a further leg kind, renaming ShellResult, or moving the tests to another hand file -- each keeps the same hand-written dispatch.",
  current_boundary: "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs (ShellResult, dispatch_shell, declared_shell_leg_ceiling, wait_child_honoring_wall_deadline, kill_shell_process_group, shell_result_of_observation, shell_result_from_capture, shell_evidence_value, mod wall_deadline_kill_tests, mod map_shell_outputs_optional_stream_tests); src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag and src/v1/05_emit.dag (the compiled-path ShellResultChannel arms); extdeps/ssh/session.dag, extdeps/ssh/password_session.dag, gunbc/typed_argv_exec.dag and the fleet wrappers (the .dag side that declares the ceiling and decodes Overran); ; src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs (enum ShellLegExec, settle_shell_stdin_writer, SHELL_STDIN_SETTLE_GRACE, and the four dispatch_shell_stdin_leg_* / outer_budget_refusal_* controls in mod argv_arg_limit_test); src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_emit.rs (struct ShellChanOverran, struct ShellChanWallDeadlineSeconds); dag/gunbc/transport_shell_wall_deadline_interpreter_seed_growth.dag"
}
